  "summary": "Prince Holding Group, a Cambodia-based conglomerate chaired by Chen Zhi, is accused by US prosecutors of running forced-labor scam compounds across Cambodia where trafficked workers ran cryptocurrency investment ('pig butchering') frauds. On 14 October 2025 the US unsealed an indictment in Brooklyn charging Chen Zhi with wire fraud conspiracy and money laundering conspiracy, filed a civil forfeiture complaint against about 127,271 bitcoin, and OFAC designated 146 targets as the Prince Group TCO in a joint action with the UK. Treasury said workers were lured by promises of well-paid customer service and tech support jobs. Chen Zhi remained at large at the time of the announcement.",
